%description:
StochasticErrorModel: parameter out of range.

packetErrorRate = 1.5 is not a probability, which the error model rejects when it is initialized.
Two ad-hoc IEEE 802.11 hosts, 20 m apart, multicast frames.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
**.radio.receiver.errorModel.typename = "StochasticErrorModel"
**.radio.receiver.errorModel.packetErrorRate = 1.5
include ../../lib/stochastic-errormodel-80211.ini

%exitcode: 1
%postrun-command: grep -h '<!>' test.out test.err > errors.out || true
%contains: errors.out
Parameter 'packetErrorRate' must be a probability in the range [0, 1] or NaN, got 1.5
